From e4f08b47494a09f2cd17bdf3a606534d4c3fd183 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 14:07:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(landing): add top nav, pricing CTAs, reorder trust strip
 above pricing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Addresses the three biggest navigation/CTA gaps on the marketing page:

1. Sticky top navigation. The page had no <header> at all — visitors
   who scrolled past the hero had no way to navigate. New TopNav:
   - Legacy Table wordmark on the left (click = scroll to top)
   - Desktop nav: How it works · Why · Pricing (smooth-scroll anchors)
   - Mobile: hamburger drawer with the same links
   - Persistent "Get the app" pill on the right

2. CTAs on every pricing tier. The pricing section previously had
   zero buttons — visitors decided to pay but couldn't act on it.
   Each card now has its own CTA:
     Free        -> "Get the free app"
     Family Plus -> "Choose Family Plus →"   (Most popular badge,
                                              accent border,
                                              slight Y-translate)
     Heirloom    -> "Choose Heirloom →"
   Tiers also gain visible $ prices and Heirloom now shows the
   $4.08/mo + "billed $49/yr — save 32%" framing instead of $49/yr,
   which obscured the value-vs-Family-Plus comparison.

3. Trust strip moved ABOVE pricing. Trust claims belong before the
   ask, not after. Added a section eyebrow ("Built for families, not
   for feeds") so the strip reads as a unit instead of an orphan row.

Adjacent fixes folded in:
- Hero CTAs renamed: "App Store" -> "Get the app", "See how it works"
  -> "What it does". Both labels now match their destinations.
- Hero subhead tightened (one fewer comma clause, adds "privately"
  to preview the trust strip and differentiate from public recipe
  sites).
- All five "App Store" buttons route through a single openAppStore()
  helper pointing at the real App Store listing
  (apps.apple.com/us/app/legacy-table/id6759821009). This is the
  hook for PR 2's platform-aware <GetTheApp /> component.
- Founder photo placeholder no longer renders alt text ("Founder
  photo") as visible body copy — replaced with a styled gradient
  placeholder + "coming soon" label until the real photo lands
  in PR 3.
- Removed the floating "Pricing built for families." line that
  sat awkwardly below the tier cards.
- "Free on iOS. Android coming soon." final-CTA sub-line replaced
  with a positive framing for iOS users ("Free on iOS. Family Plus
  and Heirloom unlock when you're ready..."). Android waitlist
  capture comes in PR 2 with the platform-aware component.
- Added scroll-mt-16 + smooth scrollIntoView so anchored sections
  don't land under the new sticky header.
- Kept the legacy <a id="features" /> alongside the new
  id="how-it-works" so any external links to the old anchor still
  work.

Not in this PR (intentional):
- Platform-aware Get the app component (PR 2)
- Android waitlist email capture (PR 2, needs backend or 3rd-party)
- Founder photo asset (PR 3)
- SEO meta tags + JSON-LD structured data (PR 3)
- Terms of Service page (PR 3)
- Mobile responsive QA on real devices

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
